      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot ({e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}+2{x}^{2}{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}) \\\\  & =2y(1+2{x}^{2}){e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
